WEBVTT

00:04:58.464 --> 00:05:01.566
DC: The interview process,
as a whole, is pretty stupid.

00:05:02.169 --> 00:05:03.825
Yeah, it's dumb.

00:05:04.945 --> 00:05:06.309
AG: It is dumb.

00:05:06.333 --> 00:05:10.059
It's dumb, in part,
because human reasoning is often dumb.

00:05:10.083 --> 00:05:12.797
Rigorous research across
nearly a century suggests

00:05:12.821 --> 00:05:14.702
that if you try to rank the performance

00:05:14.726 --> 00:05:17.153
of a hundred candidates
based on interviews,

00:05:17.177 --> 00:05:19.105
you'll be lucky if you get eight of them

00:05:19.129 --> 00:05:20.279
in the right spot.

00:05:20.938 --> 00:05:23.185
Job interviews are stuck in the past.

00:05:23.209 --> 00:05:26.331
We're still doing them the same way
they've been done for decades,

00:05:26.355 --> 00:05:28.356
and we're lagging
way behind the science,

00:05:28.380 --> 00:05:31.302
which may explain a lot
of your own experience,